            <chunk name="Object" index="34">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">671066e8-2381-4c93-b395-52c43bed6117</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">VALIDATION - Zhang &amp; Chen (2006) UFAD chamber

The underfloor-air-distribution experiment of Zhang &amp; Chen (Atmospheric Environment 40, 3396-3408, doi:10.1016/j.atmosenv.2006.01.014): a 4.91 x 4.31 x 2.44 m room, air supplied at floor level through two 0.26 m square diffusers (0.70 m/s at 20.4 / 19.9 degC) and extracted through the ceiling. Four occupants dissipate 100 W each (closed boxes carved out of the room as obstacles), six flush ceiling luminaires 64 W each, and every wall holds its measured temperature from the paper Table 2. The case solves buoyant stratified mixed convection on OpenFOAM 12 (fluid module, k-epsilon).

WHAT TO EXPECT - temperature rising continuously floor to ceiling at roughly 1.1-1.7 K/m, supply jets climbing to about 1.5 m before falling back, and thermal plumes above the occupants.

MESH - Cell Size defaults to 0.10 m for a fast first run; the paper grid was 389k cells (about 0.022 here, ~15 min on 16 cores). The quantitative validation (digitised measurements, error metrics, profile figure) lives in the Eddy3D repo: MetaFOAM.Lib.Tests / TestZhangChenUfad*.

PROVENANCE - room, loads and temperatures are the paper values; diffuser, occupant and luminaire POSITIONS are reconstructed (the paper publishes no coordinates), matching the Simvia code_saturne setup.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="4">
                        <item name="Bounds" type_name="gh_drawing_rectanglef" type_code="35">
                          <X>480</X>
                          <Y>3330</Y>
                          <W>160</W>
                          <H>100</H>
                        </item>
                        <item name="MarginLeft" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="MarginRight" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                        <item name="MarginTop" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                      </items>
                    </chunk>
                    <chunk name="PanelProperties">
                      <items count="7">
                        <item name="Colour" type_name="gh_drawing_color" type_code="36">
